WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.9 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Accountability: participation, feedback and complaints

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Let the people you serve shape the work and raise concerns, built in before habits set.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.170
Accountability means the people you serve understand what you do, help shape decisions that affect them, and can give feedback or complain, knowing it will be handled fairly.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.170
Channels for different people

5
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:36.759
Face to face: Suits people who prefer talking or read less, though some will not criticise you. For example: Chatting with parents at pick-up after each youth club session.

6
00:00:36.759 --> 00:00:46.978
Anonymous box: Suits shy or worried participants; you report back to everyone. For example: A box by the club door; answers posted on the notice board monthly.

7
00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:57.567
Phone or messaging: Suits parents and people at a distance; needs someone who answers on time. For example: A club number checked every evening, with replies within two days.

8
00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:07.874
Trusted outside person: For sensitive concerns, including safeguarding; known, trusted and briefed. For example: A retired teacher who agreed to receive concerns about the club.

9
00:01:08.274 --> 00:01:08.874
Why it matters

10
00:01:08.874 --> 00:01:14.178
1. It respects people’s dignity and their right to a say.

11
00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:19.111
2. The people you serve notice problems before you do.

12
00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:26.526
3. It is far easier to build in now than once habits are set.

13
00:01:26.926 --> 00:01:27.526
Where it leads

14
00:01:27.526 --> 00:01:31.719
1. Your feedback log, reviewed regularly for patterns.

15
00:01:31.719 --> 00:01:36.652
2. Your safeguarding procedures, in place before your first activity.

16
00:01:36.652 --> 00:01:42.956
3. Your learning reviews and reports: what changed because of feedback.

17
00:01:43.356 --> 00:01:43.956
What to avoid

18
00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:48.889
Relying on one channel that suits only some people.

19
00:01:48.889 --> 00:01:53.822
No route outside the founding team for sensitive concerns.

20
00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:59.756
Not closing the loop: people never hear what changed.

21
00:02:00.356 --> 00:02:02.156
You design your feedback and complaints mechanism.

22
00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:06.156
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:07.656 --> 00:02:10.756
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
